  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a component of the Laravel ecosystem, specifically focusing on integrating the Cashier package with Paddle's subscription billing services. Laravel Cashier Paddle serves as an abstraction layer, offering a streamlined API for Laravel applications to manage Stripe and customer subscriptions, including recurring billing operations.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to provide a fluent interface that simplifies the management of subscription billing within Laravel applications. This includes basic and advanced subscription management features, reducing the overhead of writing subscription billing code.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Individuals or teams using Laravel to build applications that require subscription billing functionality.\n- End Users: Customers who will interact with the subscription services indirectly via applications utilizing this package.\n- Business Owners: Organizations aiming to leverage subscription-based business models.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Subscription Management: Enable the creation, updating, and cancellation of customer subscriptions.\n- Subscription Swapping: Allow customers to switch between different subscription plans.\n- Quantity Management: Manage the quantities associated with customer subscriptions.\n- Subscription Pausing: Provide options to pause and resume subscriptions, with grace periods as needed.\n- Receipts: Generate and store transaction receipts with relevant details such as amounts, taxes, and currency.\n- Data Linking: Utilize a database schema to track customers, subscriptions, and receipts while maintaining referential integrity through foreign keys.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Usability: The API should be intuitive and offer a fluent interface to reduce the complexity of billing operations for developers.\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle a large number of customers and transactions.\n- Reliability: Ensure data consistency and integrity within the database, especially concerning billing operations.\n- Security: Protect sensitive customer data and secure transactions using industry-standard practices.\n- Performance: Optimize for quick response times when performing billing operations.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0087\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billable_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` char(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vat_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `customers_paddle_id_unique` (`paddle_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `paused_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `subscriptions_paddle_id_unique` (`paddle_id`),\n  KEY `subscriptions_customer_id_index` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscription_items` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `subscription_items_subscription_id_index` (`subscription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscription_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`subscription_id`) REFERENCES `subscriptions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `receipts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `receipt_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `currency` char(3) NOT NULL,\n  `subtotal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,\n  `tax` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,\n  `total` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,\n  `issued_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `receipts_paddle_id_unique` (`paddle_id`),\n  KEY `receipts_customer_id_index` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `receipts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
